add('Later hypotheses are distinguished from the original H1 and H2. H3 asks whether system-level responses persist despite implementation change; H3-M examines molecular reporter-level equivalence. H1-D and H3-D, introduced after inspection of the parallel pilots, are prospective refinements concerning protective dependency diversity at matched budgets or enhancer count, respectively. They must not be treated as tests specified before the earlier results.')
h('6. Computational experiments: reuse, fault scope and protective dependencies')
add('The studies compare matched functional portfolios within each model. Counts and costs are not pooled across models. The original benchmarks A and B address H1. The later Boolean and matrix pilots extend fault scope and dependency placement; their role is exploratory. Table and figure numbering is revised in v11; the original benchmark data are unchanged.')
