add('The companion paper’s revised v1.2 introduces H3-D as a distinct prospective question: among co-active enhancers with comparable count and activity, lower overlap of functionally supported upstream regulator dependencies may predict less endogenous target-output disruption under a nominated regulator perturbation. This concerns gene-level output, not individual reporter-fragment retention. Motif scores alone cannot establish causal upstream dependence. The two reported null multiplicity findings remain null; no H3-D outcome data have been analyzed [54].')
h('8. Cross-domain synthesis: economy, liability, independence and continuity')
sub('8.1 Functional continuity under implementation change (H3)')
region(17,78,230);fig(17,232,472,477,525);region(17,533,700)
sub('8.2 Molecular functional equivalence (H3-M)')
region(18,78,285);fig(18,289,459,463,500);region(18,507,580)
sub('8.3 Protection requires more than component count')
add('The four computational benchmarks examine different embodiments of shared dependency. A routine’s blast radius is not an enhancer’s fitness contribution, and neither is identical to a GPU’s physical fault domain. Nevertheless, a common analytical structure emerges: a functional portfolio, a dependency graph, a resource-cost vector, and an explicitly specified set of perturbations. If two protection paths share a failure source, their agreement may provide no protection against that source. The matrix pilot supplies an engineered example with matched nominal counts, while the Boolean pilot shows that changing the fault class can reverse the apparent benefit of buffering. These observations refine H1 without assuming that regulatory biology implements digital parity.')
add('For biological systems, the corresponding question is whether functionally redundant elements have distinct or shared causal dependencies. For future engineering, the corresponding question is whether complementary rather than identical protective functions can maintain output under a broader set of disturbances at a matched effective cost. Both are testable propositions; neither follows as a biological or hardware result merely from the analogy.')
# Reprise all hypothesis statuses in one table, with new refinements.
newtable('Table 10. Evidential status of the six hypotheses.', ['Hypothesis','Current evidential status','Boundary'],[['H1 — economy/liability','Supported within specified computational models','Not a universal law or biological cost result'],['H2 — reach/constraint','Negative exploratory K562 pilot','Multi-context confirmatory design remains open'],['H3 — functional continuity','Prospective system-level test','No endogenous cross-species response test'],['H3-M — molecular equivalence','Partial reported reporter-level support','Post-hoc features, margin and assay limits'],['H1-D — protection dependencies','Prospective refinement from CPU pilots','Equal effective budget and hardware test pending'],['H3-D — regulatory diversity','Prospective new biological test','No outcome data analyzed']], [138,174,180])
h('9. From genomes back to circuits: reciprocal experimental program')
sub('9.1 From sequence equivalence to pathway coordination')
region(18,632,735);region(20,600,712)
sub('9.2 Return-direction test (H1-D)')
add('At a matched effective resource and verification budget, reducing common-cause dependence between execution and checking should reduce undetected disruption for nominated fault classes. The effect may vanish for correlated upstream corruption, canceling errors, unavailable checks or expensive coordination. Compare dedicated/shared designs, conventional full duplication, weighted-checksum ABFT, independent-source baselines and a candidate inspired by biological compensatory interactions. Define a novel candidate and its biological motivation before testing; distinguish redundancy, complementary encoding and nonadditivity. Freeze workloads, resource accounting, perturbation classes, holdouts and success criteria. Report correct, wrong, unflagged wrong, flagged and missing results separately; do not optimize a single arbitrary economy score.')
sub('9.3 Actual GPU validation and reciprocal transfer')
add('Run the archived portable CUDA scaffolds first on any accessible NVIDIA device, check exact integer output, and record device SKU, driver, software versions, precision and workload. Then benchmark native kernels on H100 for cluster-local communication, TMA and shared-memory behavior, collecting repeated timings, memory traffic and profiler counters; energy only with validated instrumentation. A simulated injected error is not a field hardware failure. Use conventional engineering baselines and quantify verification and recovery overhead. Only a controlled comparison showing a reproducible advantage attributable to the proposed bio-inspired design would establish an engineering transfer. Independent reproduction, matched effective budgets and external specialist review are release gates. A negative result remains evidence, not a reason to change the expected outcome.')
diagram('reciprocal','Figure 17. Reciprocal inquiry: historical computing motivates biological hypotheses; molecular findings motivate a return-direction engineering test. Dotted return arrow marks prospective transfer, not a completed demonstration.')
h('10. Limitations, falsification criteria and conclusion')
sub('10.1 Biological and structural limitations')
region(16,306,643)
add('Additional limitations: the new pilots are construction-dependent logical models, not GPU microarchitectural simulations. They share conceptual dependencies with earlier experiments, and no physical failure distributions or performance data are available. Matched nominal counts are incomplete cost accounting; common-mode fault assumptions must be tested. The new hypotheses are post-result proposals. The reported enhancer-assay equivalence is sensitive to the margin and moderation and cannot establish system-level regulatory equivalence. No new experiments were performed for this editorial integration. Independent reproduction, code audit, full reference verification and specialist review remain outstanding.')
sub('10.2 Conclusion: functional organization through changing implementation')
add('Architectural economy connects the original PDP-8 example, modern parallel computation and biological regulatory systems by asking how a portfolio of functions is realized under resource and perturbation constraints. Reuse can reduce static cost but concentrate failure liability; protective coordination adds its own costs and dependencies. The new pilots make fault class and source independence explicit. Their contribution is a bounded refinement of the computational framework, not proof of a universal law or of physical H100 reliability.')
add('The negative K562 result is retained: higher-order reach did not positively predict sequence constraint. The companion reporter results offer partial support for molecular functional continuity, while biological economy and conserved endogenous coordination remain unestablished. The historical PDP-8 demonstrates why implementation continuity and functional continuity should be separated. Hopper provides a prospective setting for testing whether biologically motivated compensation can improve protective architecture. The essential scientific ambition is reciprocal: use computing to formulate biological questions, and use biological observations to formulate better computing questions. Preserve the question without protecting the expected answer.')
sub('Declarations and reproducibility')
region(21,457,662);region(22,60,175)
add('Version 11 editorial integration: ChatGPT assisted in restructuring and illustrating the manuscript using the preserved v9 and v10 text, figures and data, and archived parallel pilots. No new numerical analysis was run. Existing declarations require author confirmation; no independent scientific validation is claimed. The public C2G archive contains versioned source, code, results, review editions and checksums: https://github.com/RandoSY/circuits-to-genomes. The prior PDFs and release archives remain immutable. All original numerical results are retained in their original archives; new figure captions and table numbers are mapped in the v11 source and revision record.')
